# Docker Compose commands

The local stack is expected to already be running (`docker compose up`). Run Django management commands and tests inside the existing `web` container — never on the host, and never via interactive `bash`.

```bash
# ✅ GOOD
sudo docker compose exec web ./manage.py test
sudo docker compose exec web ./manage.py migrate
sudo docker compose exec web ./manage.py shell -c "..."

# ❌ BAD — host Python / interactive shell / one-off run
python manage.py test
sudo docker compose run web bash
sudo docker compose run --rm web ./manage.py test
```

Pass the full command after `web`. Prefer `exec` over `run` unless the stack is not running.
